+# l9-ci-sdk
+
+`l9-ci-sdk` is the canonical analysis and normalization SDK for Quantum-L9 CI.
+It owns provider execution/import contracts, normalized evidence and findings,
+explicit rule identity, policy classification, gate evaluation, deterministic
+artifact serialization, validation, and agent-review projections. GitHub Actions
+orchestration remains owned by `l9-ci-core`.
+
+## Current contract
+
+| Axis | Current value |
+|---|---|
+| SDK version | `1.0.0` from `l9_ci.__version__` |
+| Artifact protocol | `l9.finding-bundle/v1` |
+| Schema version | `1.0.0` |
+| Python floor | `3.11` |
+| Runtime model | source execution over `PYTHONPATH` |
+| Supported provider path | Semgrep JSON import/normalization |
+| Core pin | `f7a4ee8c1f4e4413cb3645d088cafa3e9c798235` |
+
+## Install for development
+
+The repository intentionally has no `pyproject.toml` on the current branch.
+Use a source checkout and install declared dependencies:
+
+```bash
+python3 -m venv .venv
+. .venv/bin/activate
+python -m pip install --upgrade pip
+python -m pip install -r requirements-ci.txt
+```
+
+## First use
+
+```bash
+PYTHONPATH=. python -m l9_ci --help
+PYTHONPATH=. python -m l9_ci providers list
+PYTHONPATH=. python -m l9_ci providers detect --root .
+```
+
+Core-facing commands and exit codes are defined in
+`.l9/integration-contract.yaml`. Machine-readable provider reports are the
+integration boundary. Console output is not.
+
+## Validation
+
+```bash
+ruff check .
+ruff format --check .
+mypy l9_ci
+pytest -q
+```
+
+The sealed validation report records 75 passing tests for the earlier 158-file
+bundle. The live tree has since gained CI and governance scaffolding, so that
+file count is historical until the repository gains and runs a canonical reseal
+tool.
+
+## CI and gates
+
+| Surface | Trigger | Enforcement |
+|---|---|---|
+| L9 Self CI | PR, push to `main`, dispatch | New secret findings are hard-blocking; final gate is rule-mode aware |
+| `pr_fast` analysis | Pull request, dispatch | Advisory/non-strict |
+| `merge` analysis | Push to `main`, dispatch | Advisory/non-strict |
+| `nightly` analysis | Schedule, dispatch | Advisory/non-strict |
+| `release` analysis | Tag push, dispatch | Advisory/non-strict |
+| `supply_chain` analysis | Schedule, dispatch | Advisory/non-strict |
+
+## Repository layout
+
+- `l9_ci/contracts`: immutable canonical models and enums
+- `l9_ci/providers`: provider SPI, registry, and Semgrep adapter
+- `l9_ci/repository`: deterministic repository enumeration and snapshots
+- `l9_ci/identity`: explicit canonical rule identity resolution
+- `l9_ci/policy`: policy loading and classification
+- `l9_ci/gates`: gate evaluation
+- `l9_ci/artifacts`: deterministic serialization and validation
+- `l9_ci/integration`: limits, compatibility, redaction, projections
+- `l9_ci/pipeline`: public composition flows
+- `l9_ci/commands` and `l9_ci/cli`: command composition and stable diagnostics
+- `l9_ci/schemas/v1`: ten versioned JSON schemas
+- `tests`: architecture, contracts, providers, compatibility, and integration
+- `docs/adr`: eight accepted architecture decisions plus the index
+
+## Status and known blockers
+
+Semgrep shadow rollout remains blocked on a runtime-captured redacted fixture and
+live `l9-ci-core` integration evidence. A second provider remains deferred until
+the Semgrep slice is supported without known protocol-breaking defects.
+
+## License
+
+Proprietary source-available software. See `LICENSE` before use or distribution.
